Q: Greasemonkey block cookies by wildcard A: <p>Something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const cookies = await cookieStore.getAll();
cookies.filter((cookie)=&gt;cookie.name.startsWith('Cookie')).forEach((cookie) =&gt; cookieStore.delete(cookie.name));
</code></pre>
<p>Possible since CookieStore-API:<br />
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CookieStore" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CookieStore</a></p>

Q: create a cookie with javascript in greasemonkey A: <pre><code>
var cookie_names = [
    'showDrushimPopUnderUserClick',
    'showDrushimPopUnder308'
];

cookie_names.forEach((name)=&gt;cookieStore.set(name,1);
</code></pre>
<p>If expiration dates are needed, set() accepts options too:<br />
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CookieStore/set" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CookieStore/set</a></p>
